{"skill":{"slug":"test-runner","displayName":"Test Runner"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769625021186,"changelog":"Initial release with guides for writing and running tests across major languages and frameworks:\n\n- Lists preferred test frameworks for TypeScript/JS, Python, and Swift (unit, integration, E2E).\n- Provides setup instructions and example commands for Vitest, Jest, pytest, XCTest, and Playwright.\n- Outlines common workflows (TDD) and test patterns (Arrange-Act-Assert, mocking, async).\n- Includes example snippets for testing API endpoints and UI components.\n- Documents coverage commands and strategies for both JavaScript/TypeScript and Python.\n- Clarifies “what to test” with practical recommendations.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":5091,"sha256":"2f370846f7a954fa905383dac8e07ca17943db3c3650ef77131e9200585694fb","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1734,"sha256":"fed117129e4f5fc175134079e963af5de4dafade62b481dc9994bcdfeccf38f4","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789022981278,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"60dec7f8cca3aa104575e06cec8e951d2084eac2d1063d6b9440091b969cfe3e","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/60dec7f8cca3aa104575e06cec8e951d2084eac2d1063d6b9440091b969cfe3e","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: test-runner\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle provides instructions and code snippets for setting up and running tests across various programming languages and frameworks. All commands and dependencies listed are standard for testing tools (e.g., `npm install`, `npx vitest`, `pytest`, `playwright`). There is no evidence of prompt injection against the agent, data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or obfuscation. The content is clearly aligned with its stated purpose of running tests.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160229401},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":16,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":15,"checkedAt":1789022981278},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a straightforward testing guide with disclosed commands; its main risk is that some example installs and npx commands are not version-pinned.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Running test frameworks and coverage tools is proportionate to the skill’s purpose, and the examples do not request elevated privileges or broad filesystem indexing beyond ordinary project test execution.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"There is no separate installer or executable package in the artifact, but the guide recommends unpinned npm and uv dependency installs plus unpinned npx commands, which users should treat as normal package-manager supply-chain exposure.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The instructions are documentation-style examples for test setup, test execution, TDD, and coverage; I found no prompt hijacking, hidden role changes, credential handling, destructive actions, or unrelated agent directives.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact does not install background services, scheduled tasks, persistent hooks, shell profile changes, memory rules, or privilege escalation mechanisms.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact’s stated purpose is to write and run tests across common frameworks, and the content stays within testing workflows for Vitest, Jest, pytest, XCTest, and Playwright.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before using the commands, prefer project-local pinned devDependencies, committed lockfiles, and npm/uv frozen install workflows. Run tests in a least-privileged development or CI environment without production secrets when possible.","findings":"[RP1] expected: The repeated unpinned npx examples for Vitest, Jest, and Playwright are present and represent a real supply-chain caution, but they are visible, testing-related commands rather than hidden or purpose-mismatched behavior.\n[T08] expected: The unpinned third-party dependency install finding is supported by the artifact, but the named packages are standard test tooling and no artifact evidence shows malicious packages, deception, persistence, or exfiltration.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789022981278}}}}}